# Phase 18 MessageExt flag override follow-up — 2026-10-21T18:47:26Z

Branch: `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`
Code revision: `a24fba3a` (`feat(common): dispatch MessageExt subtype flags`)
Pinned Java source: `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.
Fixture SHA-256: `8afd6c83b5085d3c74cbcdd919bca3257514abbde3c7f3ec70847dd08a1a2f7f`.

## Source audit and change

- Java `Message.getFlag()` and `setFlag(int)` are virtual. Push retry and
  send-back paths read `msg.getFlag()` when creating retry messages. Rust
  previously resolved `MessageExt::flag()` and `set_flag()` through the base
  `Message` fields, ignoring caller-defined subtype overrides.
- Added `MessageExtSubtype` hooks for `getFlag` and `setFlag`; `MessageExt`
  now dispatches those methods and falls back to its stored base message when
  the subtype uses the defaults.
- The invoked Java custom subtype returns flag `71` and counts setter calls.
  The direct-consume fixture invokes `setFlag(5)` and records the callback's
  flag. Rust compares the callback value and custom setter count. The runtime
  fixture now emits the flag for all 27 direct-consume cases.
- Updated the Phase 6, Phase 10 and Phase 18 compatibility records and the
  release checklist. Arbitrary subtype overrides and the broader P18-V01
  audit remain open.

